<Chapter id="ch-04" num="04" end="say yes before you know how.">
  <Phones slot="graphic" />
  <p class="beat">My first job was junior graphic designer. The pay was bad enough that freelancing looked safer, so I messaged everyone I'd ever worked with and offered a friendly rate. It turns out a friendly rate is mostly friendly to them.</p>
  <p class="beat">Audio one month, video the next, scripts after that. The range was the product.</p>
  <p class="beat">Then a client said: you're good at Photoshop, can you design the screens for my app?</p>
  <p class="beat">I had no background in UX.</p>
  <div class="beat-gap" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p class="beat-h">So naturally, I said yes.</p>
  <p class="beat">Then I learned UX. I don't see it as changing disciplines. It was the same job in a different mode.</p>
  <ToolTag tool="UX" />
</Chapter>
